(window.FREE_Q = window.FREE_Q || {})["xxv-a"] = {"qs": [["Research Reporting, Ethics & Regulation", "SEBI's Centralised Fee Collection Mechanism (CeFCoM) for research analysts helps clients by:", ["Guaranteeing a minimum return on all research recommendations", "Letting clients pay fees in cash at any bank branch", "Ensuring fees are paid only to registered research analysts", "Allowing unregistered entities to collect fees"], 2, "CeFCoM routes fee payments through a mechanism that verifies the recipient is a registered RA, protecting clients from paying unregistered or fraudulent entities."], ["Risk and Return Fundamentals", "Which statement about diversification is correct?", ["It reduces company-specific risk but not market risk", "It removes all types of investment risk completely", "It increases risk because more stocks are held", "It works only for government bonds and not for equities"], 0, "Holding many different securities offsets company-specific shocks, but market-wide events such as recessions or rate changes affect all stocks. That systematic risk remains."], ["Research Fundamentals & Market Analysis", "A company's operating profit margin is calculated as:", ["Net profit divided by total shareholders' equity", "Total debt divided by shareholders' equity", "Dividends divided by net profit", "Operating profit divided by revenue"], 3, "Operating margin = operating profit (EBIT) ÷ revenue, showing how much of each rupee of sales remains after operating costs. The other options are ROE, debt-equity and payout ratio."], ["Risk and Return Fundamentals", "Standard deviation as a risk measure treats:", ["Only losses below zero as risk", "Upside and downside deviations equally", "Only the single worst day as risk", "Only dividends as a source of risk"], 1, "Standard deviation measures dispersion around the average in both directions. Measures like downside deviation focus only on returns below a target."], ["Research Profession & Securities Markets", "A research analyst registered with SEBI can be:", ["An individual, partnership firm or body corporate", "Only a listed company with net worth above ₹100 crore", "Only an individual working from home", "Only a stock exchange or depository"], 0, "SEBI's Research Analysts Regulations allow registration of individuals, partnership firms, LLPs and bodies corporate, each meeting qualification, certification and net worth or deposit requirements."], ["Research Reporting, Ethics & Regulation", "Under SEBI's amended Research Analyst framework, if a research analyst uses AI tools in preparing research services, it must:", ["Avoid any disclosure, since AI tools are confidential business secrets", "Transfer responsibility for the research to the AI tool's provider", "Disclose the use and remain responsible for the output", "Obtain separate SEBI registration for the AI tool itself"], 2, "The amended framework requires research analysts to disclose the extent of AI use to clients and holds them solely responsible for data security, confidentiality and the integrity of the output."], ["Client Interaction & Relationship Skills", "When a client complains about a delayed report delivery, the sales staff should:", ["Log the complaint and update the client on resolution", "Tell the client to file a police complaint", "Ignore the complaint if the client is a small subscriber", "Delete the complaint from the system"], 0, "All complaints should be recorded and tracked to resolution, with the client kept informed. Records also help the firm meet regulatory grievance reporting obligations."], ["Research Reporting, Ethics & Regulation", "If a research analyst does not resolve a client's complaint, the client may escalate it:", ["First to SCORES, then to online dispute resolution", "Only to a civil court in the analyst's city", "To the client's bank manager", "To the stock exchange's listing department"], 0, "Clients of SEBI-registered RAs can lodge complaints on SCORES and, if unsatisfied, initiate online dispute resolution through the Smart ODR portal."], ["Research Fundamentals & Market Analysis", "Price-to-earnings (P/E) ratios are usually not meaningful for a company that:", ["Has negative earnings", "Pays regular dividends every year", "Has a market capitalisation above ₹1 lakh crore", "Is part of the Nifty 50 index"], 0, "If earnings are negative, the P/E ratio is negative or undefined and cannot be compared. Analysts may use price-to-sales or EV/EBITDA instead for loss-making firms."], ["Research Profession & Securities Markets", "A client asks what the 'free float' of a company means. A correct explanation is:", ["The total number of shares the company is legally permitted to issue in future", "Shares that the company gives away free to employees each year", "The cash balance held by the company in its bank accounts", "Shares readily available for trading, excluding promoter holdings"], 3, "Free float excludes shares held by promoters, government and other locked-in holders. Many indices, including the Nifty 50, use free-float market capitalisation for weighting."], ["Professional Efficiency & Tools", "A sales executive spends most of the day replying to routine internal chats and keeps missing scheduled client callbacks. The most effective fix is to:", ["Reply to every internal chat instantly, since quick replies show commitment", "Stop making client callbacks and rely on clients to call back themselves", "Block time for priority tasks and batch routine messages", "Work late every night instead of changing how the day is organised"], 2, "Time-blocking protects important work such as client callbacks, while batching routine messages reduces constant interruptions. Working longer hours or dropping callbacks does not address the real problem of poor prioritisation."], ["Client Interaction & Relationship Skills", "A client calls angrily after a recommended stock falls. A good first step for the sales staff is to:", ["Blame the analyst who wrote the report in front of the client", "Listen calmly and acknowledge the client's concern", "Promise the client that the firm will compensate all losses", "End the call quickly and avoid further contact"], 1, "Active listening and empathy defuse tension. Staff can then share the analyst's updated view and the reasons, without blaming colleagues or making promises."], ["Research Reporting, Ethics & Regulation", "For individual and HUF clients, SEBI's amended framework limits the fees a research analyst may collect in advance to:", ["Fees for a period of up to one quarter", "Fees for up to ten years in a single lump sum", "Fees for the client's whole lifetime", "Any amount, as long as the client agrees"], 0, "To protect retail clients, SEBI allows RAs to collect advance fees from individual and HUF clients for at most one quarter. Longer advance collection is not permitted."], ["Client Interaction & Relationship Skills", "A client wants to put all savings into one small-cap stock from a research report. The sales executive should:", ["Encourage it, since the report is positive on the stock", "Point out concentration risk and the report's risk disclosures", "Offer the client a discount on fees for doing so", "Tell the client that small caps are risk-free"], 1, "While sales staff do not give personal advice, they should communicate the risks highlighted in research and avoid encouraging behaviour that exposes the client to excessive risk."], ["Client Interaction & Relationship Skills", "A long-standing client asks for early access to a research report before it is released to other clients. The staff should:", ["Agree, since loyal clients deserve special treatment", "Share a summary of the report in a personal message", "Agree if the client pays an extra fee", "Decline, as reports must be shared fairly with clients"], 3, "Research must be distributed fairly to all eligible clients at the same time. Selective early sharing disadvantages other clients and may enable trading on unpublished information."], ["Professional Efficiency & Tools", "A sales executive wants to use a personal messaging app to share research with clients because it is convenient. The firm's policy should ensure that:", ["Only approved, recorded channels are used", "Any messaging app may be used as long as clients do not complain", "Personal phones may be used without any record of messages", "Messages should be deleted after sending to save space"], 0, "Firms must keep records of client communications. Using approved channels ensures recording, supervision and data security, which unrecorded personal apps cannot provide."], ["Professional Efficiency & Tools", "Which is the strongest password practice for systems holding client data?", ["Sharing one password among the team for convenience", "Unique passwords with multi-factor authentication", "Using the same password for all systems and personal e-mail", "Writing passwords on a note attached to the monitor"], 1, "Unique, strong passwords combined with multi-factor authentication greatly reduce the risk of unauthorised access. Sharing or reusing passwords creates serious vulnerabilities."], ["Research Profession & Securities Markets", "The secondary market's main function for investors is to:", ["Provide liquidity by letting investors trade existing securities", "Let companies raise fresh capital directly from the public through IPOs", "Fix the interest rates on bank deposits each month", "Approve new research analyst registrations"], 0, "The secondary market lets investors buy and sell already-issued securities, providing liquidity and price discovery. Fresh capital is raised in the primary market."], ["Client Interaction & Relationship Skills", "A prospective client asks whether subscribing to research will guarantee profits. The best response is to:", ["Assure him that most subscribers double their money within a year", "Tell him profits are guaranteed if he follows every call strictly", "Avoid answering and ask him to pay the fee first", "Explain that research improves decisions but profits are not guaranteed"], 3, "Honest communication is essential when selling research. Research can inform decisions, but markets are uncertain and no outcome or profit can be guaranteed to any client."], ["Client Interaction & Relationship Skills", "A client tells the sales executive confidential details about his business. The executive should:", ["Share it with colleagues for gossip", "Post it on social media as a success story", "Pass it on to other clients as a tip", "Keep it confidential and use it only for servicing"], 3, "Client information must be kept confidential and used only for legitimate purposes. Misuse breaches ethics, data protection norms and possibly insider trading rules."], ["Research Profession & Securities Markets", "A client asks why derivatives volumes in India are very high compared with cash market volumes. A balanced response is:", ["Derivatives are completely risk-free and therefore extremely popular", "Cash market trades are banned for retail investors", "Derivatives need only margin, so notional turnover is large", "SEBI guarantees profits in derivatives trades"], 2, "Futures and options are traded on margin, so the notional value traded is many times the capital deployed. SEBI studies show most individual F&O traders lose money."], ["Professional Efficiency & Tools", "Under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, a research firm should collect client personal data:", ["In as much detail as possible for future marketing", "Without telling the client how it will be used", "And sell it to third parties for revenue", "Only for a specified lawful purpose"], 3, "The DPDP Act requires personal data to be processed for lawful purposes with consent or legitimate use, limited to what is necessary, and protected with reasonable safeguards."], ["Client Interaction & Relationship Skills", "A client repeatedly checks prices and wants to sell after every small dip. This behaviour mostly reflects:", ["Loss aversion and short-term focus", "Disciplined long-term investing", "Efficient use of a research report", "The disposition effect of holding losers"], 0, "Over-reacting to small losses reflects loss aversion and myopic focus. Staff can remind the client of the research horizon and the report's risk disclosures."], ["Risk and Return Fundamentals", "A stock with beta of 0.6 is best described as:", ["Twice as volatile as the market at all times", "Less volatile than the market, on average", "Completely free of market risk", "Guaranteed to rise when the market falls"], 1, "A beta below 1 means the stock tends to move less than the market. It still carries market risk and does not necessarily move opposite to the market."], ["Research Fundamentals & Market Analysis", "A company has current assets of ₹240 crore and current liabilities of ₹160 crore. Its current ratio is:", ["1.5", "0.67", "2.4", "4.0"], 0, "Current ratio = current assets ÷ current liabilities = 240 ÷ 160 = 1.5. It indicates the firm's ability to meet short-term obligations from short-term assets."], ["Professional Efficiency & Tools", "A CRM system helps a research firm's sales team by:", ["Generating research recommendations automatically without analysts", "Tracking client interactions, requests and follow-ups", "Guaranteeing that every prospect becomes a paying client", "Replacing the need for KYC procedures"], 1, "CRM tools centralise client information and interaction history, improving service and follow-up. They do not produce research or replace KYC."], ["Risk and Return Fundamentals", "A dividend of ₹8 on a share bought at ₹200, which is now ₹210, gives a total return of:", ["5%", "9%", "4%", "4.2%"], 1, "Total return = (price gain + dividend) ÷ cost = (10 + 8) ÷ 200 = 9%. Price return alone is 5%, and dividend yield on cost is 4%."], ["Risk and Return Fundamentals", "A portfolio returned 14% with standard deviation 16%; the risk-free rate is 6%. Its Sharpe ratio is:", ["0.875", "1.25", "0.50", "0.375"], 2, "Sharpe ratio = (14 − 6) ÷ 16 = 0.50. It measures excess return per unit of total risk, helping compare portfolios with different volatility."], ["Risk and Return Fundamentals", "A client sees that a research report's model portfolio fell 30% from its peak before recovering. This peak-to-trough fall is called:", ["Maximum drawdown", "Tracking error relative to the benchmark", "Dividend yield on the portfolio", "Expense ratio of the portfolio"], 0, "Maximum drawdown measures the largest fall from a peak to a subsequent trough. It helps clients understand how bad losses have been in the past."], ["Professional Efficiency & Tools", "A sales executive drafts client e-mails with a public generative AI tool. To stay compliant, she should:", ["Paste the client's full portfolio and PAN for better results", "Send the AI output to clients without reading it", "Use the AI tool to create new stock recommendations", "Avoid entering personal or confidential client data"], 3, "Public AI tools may store inputs, risking data leaks. Staff should not share confidential data, must review outputs and must never use AI to generate unapproved recommendations."], ["Research Reporting, Ethics & Regulation", "A research analyst has published a buy recommendation on a stock. Personal trading by the analyst against that recommendation is:", ["Allowed at any time, since it is the analyst's own money", "Allowed if the analyst informs the sales team verbally", "Prohibited for the restricted period around the report", "Required to show independence"], 2, "SEBI restricts RAs and their associates from dealing in recommended securities during specified periods before and after publication, and from trading against their own recommendations."], ["Research Reporting, Ethics & Regulation", "A research analyst firm sends a WhatsApp message saying a stock 'will double in 3 months, guaranteed'. This is:", ["Allowed, if the stock actually doubles later", "Allowed, if sent only to existing clients", "Prohibited, since assured or guaranteed returns cannot be promised", "Allowed for model portfolios"], 2, "SEBI prohibits research analysts from guaranteeing or assuring returns. Such statements mislead clients and may also amount to market manipulation."], ["Research Profession & Securities Markets", "Persons associated with research services who handle sales and other non-core functions are required to hold:", ["A licence from the stock exchange as a sub-broker", "The NISM Series V-A mutual fund distributor certificate only", "A chartered financial analyst charter in all cases", "The NISM Series XXV-A certification"], 3, "SEBI requires persons associated with research services in sales and other non-core roles to obtain the NISM Series XXV-A certification. Research analysts themselves need NISM Series XV."], ["Research Profession & Securities Markets", "Which activity is a core research function rather than a sales or support function?", ["Onboarding new clients and completing their KYC formalities", "Explaining the subscription plans and fees to prospects", "Handling client queries about login and report delivery", "Preparing a valuation and target price for a stock"], 3, "Analysis, valuation and recommendations are core research functions performed by research analysts. Onboarding, fee explanation and service queries are non-core activities."], ["Risk and Return Fundamentals", "A client says, 'This stock has never fallen, so it's safe.' The most appropriate response is that:", ["The stock is risk-free because it has not fallen before", "Past performance does not guarantee future results", "SEBI guarantees stocks that have never fallen", "Only bonds can fall in value"], 1, "Any equity can fall in future, whatever its history. Research communications must make clear that past performance is not indicative of future returns."], ["Research Fundamentals & Market Analysis", "In technical analysis, a 'support level' is a price level where:", ["The company's management has promised to buy back shares", "SEBI has fixed a minimum price for the stock", "Buying interest has tended to stop the price falling", "The stock's book value per share is exactly equal to price"], 2, "Support is an area where demand has historically been strong enough to halt declines. It can break, and it is not a guaranteed floor."], ["Professional Efficiency & Tools", "Continuing professional education is important for persons associated with research services mainly because:", ["Regulations, products and markets keep changing", "It allows them to issue their own research reports", "It replaces the need for NISM certification", "It guarantees higher returns for clients"], 0, "Keeping knowledge current helps staff explain research accurately and comply with evolving rules. It does not authorise them to perform core research functions."], ["Research Profession & Securities Markets", "Which body administers and supervises research analysts on behalf of SEBI?", ["The Association of Mutual Funds in India acting on its own", "The Reserve Bank of India's financial markets department", "A recognised Research Analyst Administration and Supervisory Body", "The Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India"], 2, "SEBI has recognised a RAASB (BSE) to administer and supervise research analysts, including enlistment, monitoring and grievance handling. AMFI, RBI and IRDAI have no role here."], ["Risk and Return Fundamentals", "A share bought at ₹400 is worth ₹576 after 2 years with no dividends. Its CAGR is:", ["22%", "20%", "44%", "18%"], 1, "CAGR = (576 / 400)^(1/2) − 1 = (1.44)^0.5 − 1 = 1.2 − 1 = 20%. Dividing the 44% total gain by two gives 22%, which ignores compounding."], ["Research Fundamentals & Market Analysis", "An 'inverted yield curve' is often watched by analysts because it:", ["Always signals that inflation will fall to zero within a year", "Has historically been associated with economic slowdowns", "Means that long-term bonds have no interest rate risk", "Shows that share prices will rise in the next quarter"], 1, "When short-term yields exceed long-term yields, it often reflects expectations of rate cuts due to weaker growth. It is a signal, not a certainty."], ["Research Profession & Securities Markets", "A sales executive at a SEBI-registered research analyst firm wants to tell a client which stock to buy based on her own view. She should:", ["Give her own buy call, since she understands the client better than the analyst does", "Give the call only on WhatsApp so that no record of the advice is created", "Share only the firm's published research, not personal recommendations", "Give personal calls only to clients whose fees have been paid in advance"], 2, "Recommendations must come from qualified research analysts through approved research. Non-core staff can distribute and explain published research but must not issue their own calls."], ["Research Reporting, Ethics & Regulation", "A research report must include disclosures about:", ["The personal phone numbers of every client who will receive the report", "The analyst's family members' salaries and bank balances", "The analyst's financial interests and conflicts in the company", "The share prices of all companies outside the sector"], 2, "Reports must disclose material conflicts, such as holdings in the subject company, compensation received from it and other relationships, so clients can judge objectivity."], ["Research Fundamentals & Market Analysis", "A sharp depreciation of the rupee is most likely to benefit which sector?", ["Oil marketing companies that import most of their crude oil", "Airlines that pay for fuel and aircraft leases in dollars", "Companies with large unhedged foreign currency loans", "IT services companies that earn mainly in US dollars"], 3, "Exporters earning in foreign currency get more rupees per dollar when the rupee weakens. Importers and firms with unhedged foreign debt see costs rise."], ["Research Reporting, Ethics & Regulation", "Research analysts must maintain records of research reports and client communications for at least:", ["Six months", "Five years", "One year", "Three months"], 1, "SEBI requires RAs to preserve records such as research reports, recommendations, client KYC and communications for a minimum of five years."], ["Research Fundamentals & Market Analysis", "A rise in the government's fiscal deficit financed by heavy borrowing may lead to:", ["An automatic fall in inflation to below 2% in every case", "Lower corporate taxes for all listed companies", "An immediate rise in all share prices", "Higher bond yields as government borrowing grows"], 3, "Heavy government borrowing increases the supply of bonds and can push up yields, raising borrowing costs. The effect on equities and inflation depends on many factors."], ["Client Interaction & Relationship Skills", "Which practice by sales staff amounts to pressure selling?", ["Sending the prospect a clear fee schedule and terms to review", "Telling a prospect the 'offer ends tonight' to force a quick decision", "Answering the prospect's questions about the research process", "Giving the prospect time to read the client agreement"], 1, "Pressure selling uses artificial urgency or fear to push decisions. Clients should be given time and full information to decide."], ["Professional Efficiency & Tools", "A staff member receives an e-mail appearing to be from the CEO asking for client data urgently via a personal e-mail address. The best response is to:", ["Send the data immediately because the CEO asked", "Forward the e-mail to all clients for their information", "Verify the request through a separate known channel first", "Reply with the data but mark it confidential"], 2, "This is a typical phishing or impersonation pattern. Verifying through a known channel prevents data leaks, and the incident should be reported to IT security."], ["Research Fundamentals & Market Analysis", "Which source should research staff rely on for official corporate announcements of listed companies?", ["Messages forwarded in social media investment groups", "Comments posted on unverified discussion forums", "Rumours heard from other market participants", "Filings on stock exchange websites"], 3, "Listed companies must disclose material information through stock exchanges, which makes exchange filings the authoritative source. Unverified social media content can be inaccurate or even deliberately manipulative."]]};
